<doc>Input file and visual extraction configuration for the Life Cycle
module. The expected stage, capability, and business-model structure is
read from the existing Module_LifeCycle object in TARGET_FILE.</doc>
{MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE}
    = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Servitization_LifeCycle.pdf"

If {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE} is not empty:

    <doc>All coordinates below apply only after the page has been
    rotated into its normal reading orientation and any perspective
    distortion has been corrected.</doc>

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_TITLE_AREA} =
        x between 0% and 100%,
        y between 0% and 9%

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_STAGE_HEADER_AREA} =
        x between 15% and 98%,
        y between 8% and 28%

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_BUSINESS_MODEL_HEADER_AREA} =
        x between 15% and 98%,
        y between 27% and 35%

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_CAPABILITY_LABEL_AREA} =
        x between 5% and 15%,
        y between 34% and 100%

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA} =
        x between 15% and 98%,
        y between 34% and 100%


    <doc>Module-specific anchors used to choose the correct page
    orientation. The expected text values and collection sizes come
    from the existing target object and are not duplicated here.</doc>
    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ORIENTATION_ANCHORS} =

        The existing Module_LifeCycle.headline appears horizontally near the top of the page.

        Existing LifeCycleStage.name values appear as stage headings ordered from left to right.

        Existing BusinessCapability.name values appear as capability
        labels ordered from top to bottom.

        Existing BusinessModelArgument.businessModel values appear as
        business-model headings.

        Printed Pro and Contra labels are upright.

        The lifecycle matrix contains consistent horizontal and
        vertical grid lines.

        The number of visual stage columns corresponds to the number of
        existing LifeCycleStage objects.

        Within each stage, the number of visual capability bands
        corresponds to the number of existing BusinessCapability
        objects.

        Within each capability, the number of visual business-model
        subcolumns corresponds to the number of existing
        BusinessModelArgument objects.


    <doc>Grid lines and printed headings determine the exact internal
    cell boundaries. The configured areas above are mandatory outer
    search boundaries, not replacements for detected grid lines.</doc>

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_STAGE_BOUNDARY_RULE} =
        Detect stage boundaries from vertical grid lines inside
        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA}.

        If an internal stage divider cannot be detected, divide the
        unresolved width according to the ordered number of existing
        LifeCycleStage objects in TARGET_FILE.

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_CAPABILITY_BOUNDARY_RULE} =
        Detect capability boundaries from horizontal grid lines inside
        each detected stage area.

        If an internal capability divider cannot be detected, divide
        the unresolved height according to the ordered number of
        existing BusinessCapability objects in the matched
        LifeCycleStage.

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_BUSINESS_MODEL_BOUNDARY_RULE} =
        Detect business-model boundaries from vertical grid lines and
        printed business-model headings inside each capability area.

        If an internal business-model divider cannot be detected,
        divide the unresolved width according to the ordered number of
        existing BusinessModelArgument objects in the matched
        BusinessCapability.

    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_BOUNDARY_RULE} =
        Detect the boundary between Pro and Contra from the horizontal
        grid line or printed Pro and Contra labels.

        If that boundary cannot be detected, use the upper half as Pro
        and the lower half as Contra.

