<doc>Here you define the read area for the Staged Offering Portfolio module. You have to use coordinates, because simple descriptions are not accurate enough</doc>
If {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} is not empty:
    For {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE}:
        Rotate the picture 90° counterclockwise before OCR and before applying any read-area instructions.
    {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_READ_AREA_01} = All post-its sticking in following rectangle area: x between 0% and 33%, y between 0% and 100%
    {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_READ_AREA_02} = All post-its sticking in following rectangle area: x between 33% and 66%, y between 0% and 100%
    {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_READ_AREA_03} = All post-its sticking in following rectangle area: x between 66% and 100%, y between 0% and 100%

<doc>Here you define the read area for the Roadmap module.</doc>
If {MD_ROADMAP_FILE} is not empty:
    {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA} = Rectangle area within {MD_ROADMAP_FILE} with a picture as background.
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H3_01} = Upper left quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H3_02} = Upper center quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H3_03} = Upper right quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H2_01} = Middle left quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H2_02} = Middle center quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H2_03} = Middle right quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H1_01} = Lower left quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H1_02} = Lower center quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}
    {MD_ROADMAP_QUADRANT_H1_03} = Lower right quadrant of {MD_ROADMAP_READ_AREA}


<doc>Here you only update the already exting {TARGET_FILE} that has been created in the 'prefill' step. We use the properties of {TARGET_FILE} directly to clearly instruct the LLM for mapping.</doc>
EXECUTION:

Structure for the data mapping = {JSON_SCHEMA}:


<doc>Populate the existing Module_LifeCycle from the configured
lifecycle poster.</doc>
If {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE} is not empty:

    Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_LifeCycle

    Render every page of {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE}.

    Run the common orientation and geometry normalization process using {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ORIENTATION_ANCHORS}.

    Use the resulting {NORMALIZED_DOCUMENT_IMAGE} for every subsequent operation.

    Confirm that:
        the main title is horizontal
        the six stage headings run from left to right
        capability rows run from top to bottom
        CAPEX appears left of OPEX
        Pro appears above Contra

    If these conditions are not satisfied:
        Stop lifecycle extraction.
        Report that lifecycle orientation normalization failed.

    <doc>Constrain heading detection to the configured header areas.</doc>
    Detect lifecycle-stage headings only inside {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_STAGE_HEADER_AREA}.

    Detect CAPEX and OPEX headings only inside {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_BUSINESS_MODEL_HEADER_AREA}.

    Detect argument post-its only inside {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA}.

    Do not extract post-its from outside {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA}.

    <doc>Determine exact matrix geometry.</doc>
    Detect the vertical grid lines that divide the argument matrix into six stage columns.

    Detect the horizontal grid lines that divide the argument matrix into three capability bands and their Pro and Contra cells.

    Use detected grid lines as the primary boundaries.

    If an individual grid line cannot be detected reliably:
        Use the corresponding configured {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_STAGE_COLUMN_XX} or {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_CAPABILITY_BAND_XX} as its fallback boundary.

    Do not replace all detected grid lines with approximate coordinate boundaries merely because one grid line is unclear.

    Confirm that the resulting matrix has:
        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_EXPECTED_STAGE_COUNT} stage columns
        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_EXPECTED_CAPABILITY_COUNT} capability bands per stage
        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_EXPECTED_BUSINESS_MODEL_COUNT} business-model areas per capability
        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_EXPECTED_ARGUMENT_TYPE_COUNT} argument cells per business model

    If the resulting matrix does not have this topology:
        Stop lifecycle extraction.
        Report the detected topology and the expected topology.

    <doc>Match detected stage columns to existing stage objects.</doc>
    For each detected stage column from left to right:

        Read its printed heading from {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_STAGE_HEADER_AREA}.

        Match it to one existing LifeCycleStage in:
            {TARGET_FILE}.module_LifeCycle.lifeCycleStage

        Normalize heading comparison by:
            trimming whitespace
            converting to lowercase
            applying Unicode NFC
            replacing line breaks with spaces
            treating "&" and "and" as equivalent
            ignoring repeated spaces
            ignoring punctuation differences

        Apply this known alias:
            Poster:
                "Decommissioning End of Life Treatment"
            Existing target:
                "Deommissioning & End of Life Treatment"

        If the heading is covered or not sufficiently legible:
            Use its left-to-right position as fallback:

                For each LifeCycleStage in {TARGET_FILE}.module_LifeCycle
                    
                    Column XX =
                        LifeCycleStage.name

        Set:
            {STAGE_AREA}
                = intersection of:
                    matched detected stage column
                    {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA}

        Do not create a new LifeCycleStage.
        Do not change the matched LifeCycleStage id, name, or
        description.

        <doc>Match capability rows within the stage.</doc>
        For each detected capability band from top to bottom:

            Match it to one existing BusinessCapability in:
                LifeCycleStage.businessCapability

            Use the side banners, printed capability labels, configured
            capability names, and row position.

            Apply these aliases:

                Poster:
                    "Shopfloor Operations"
                Target:
                    "Shopfloor Operations"

                Poster:
                    "Business Operations (€)"
                Target:
                    "Business Operations"

                Poster:
                    "Service Provider Customer Manager"
                Target:
                    "Service Provider / Customer Manager"

            If the capability label is covered or not sufficiently
            legible:

                For each BusinessCapability in {TARGET_FILE}.businessParty
                
                Band XX =
                    BusinessCapability.name

            Set:
                {CAPABILITY_AREA}
                    = intersection of:
                        {STAGE_AREA}
                        matched detected capability band
                        corresponding configured
                        {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_CAPABILITY_BAND_XX}

            Do not create a new BusinessCapability.
            Do not change its id or name.

            <doc>Divide the capability area into CAPEX and OPEX.</doc>
            Use the detected CAPEX/OPEX divider as the primary
            boundary.

            If that divider is covered or unclear:
                Divide {CAPABILITY_AREA} vertically into equal halves.

            Set:
                {CAPEX_AREA}
                    = left business-model area of {CAPABILITY_AREA}

                {OPEX_AREA}
                    = right business-model area of {CAPABILITY_AREA}

            Match:
                BusinessModelArgument.businessModel = "CAPEX"
                    to {CAPEX_AREA}

                BusinessModelArgument.businessModel = "OPEX"
                    to {OPEX_AREA}

            Do not infer CAPEX or OPEX from post-it color.

            Do not change the businessModel value.

            <doc>Divide each business-model area into Pro and Contra
            cells.</doc>
            For each matched BusinessModelArgument:

                If businessModel = "CAPEX":
                    {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA} = {CAPEX_AREA}

                If businessModel = "OPEX":
                    {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA} = {OPEX_AREA}

                Detect the printed Pro/Contra separator or horizontal
                grid line.

                If the separator is detected:
                    {PRO_CELL}
                        = portion of {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA} above the
                          detected separator

                    {CONTRA_CELL}
                        = portion of {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA} below the
                          detected separator

                Else:
                    {PRO_CELL}
                        = upper half of {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA}

                    {CONTRA_CELL}
                        = lower half of {BUSINESS_MODEL_AREA}

                Intersect both cells with
                {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_ARGUMENT_MATRIX_AREA}.

                <doc>Extract Pro Argument.</doc>
                Detect all physical post-its overlapping {PRO_CELL}.

                Assign a post-it to {PRO_CELL} only when:
                    its center lies inside {PRO_CELL}; or
                    its largest overlap is with {PRO_CELL}

                If the largest overlap with two cells is approximately
                equal:
                    Mark the post-it as ambiguous.
                    Do not map it automatically.

                From post-its assigned to {PRO_CELL}, retain only actual
                handwritten post-its containing handwritten content.

                Ignore:
                    printed template squares
                    printed thumbs-up or thumbs-down icons
                    masking tape
                    transparent tape
                    grey covered areas
                    shadows
                    grid borders
                    printed "Pro Argument" text
                    printed headings
                    blank post-its without handwriting

                Do not use post-it color as a semantic signal.

                If exactly one handwritten post-it containing content is
                present:
                    Extract its handwritten text using the global
                    post-it rules.

                    Preserve meaningful standalone symbols such as "$".

                    If BusinessModelArgument.proArgument is absent:
                        {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1

                        Create PostIt with:
                            id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                            note = extracted handwritten text

                        set BusinessModelArgument.proArgument = PostIt

                    Else:
                        retain BusinessModelArgument.proArgument.id
                        replace BusinessModelArgument.proArgument.note
                            with the extracted handwritten text

                If no handwritten content is present:
                    Do not create proArgument.
                    Do not increment {NOTE_COUNTER}.

                    If proArgument already exists from an earlier
                    extraction:
                        Do not delete it automatically.
                        Report a source/target discrepancy.

                If more than one handwritten post-it containing content
                is present:
                    Do not merge their texts.
                    Do not select one silently.
                    Report an ambiguity because proArgument is singular.

                <doc>Extract Contra Argument.</doc>
                Apply the identical procedure to {CONTRA_CELL}.

                If exactly one handwritten post-it containing content is
                present:
                    Extract its handwritten text using the global
                    post-it rules.

                    Preserve meaningful standalone symbols such as "$".

                    If BusinessModelArgument.contraArgument is absent:
                        {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1

                        Create PostIt with:
                            id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                            note = extracted handwritten text

                        set BusinessModelArgument.contraArgument = PostIt

                    Else:
                        retain BusinessModelArgument.contraArgument.id
                        replace
                            BusinessModelArgument.contraArgument.note
                            with the extracted handwritten text

                If no handwritten content is present:
                    Do not create contraArgument.
                    Do not increment {NOTE_COUNTER}.

                    If contraArgument already exists from an earlier
                    extraction:
                        Do not delete it automatically.
                        Report a source/target discrepancy.

                If more than one handwritten post-it containing content
                is present:
                    Do not merge their texts.
                    Do not select one silently.
                    Report an ambiguity because contraArgument is
                    singular.


<doc>Populate Free Association by reading all post-its in the configured area and appending as PostIt notes.</doc>
If {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_FreeAssociation.freeAssociation
        
        Extract text from each post-it in {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

        For each post-it extracted:
            {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
            PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                append PostIt to {TARGET_FILE}.module_FreeAssociation.freeAssociation


<doc>Populate Different Views Rated by pairing idea/problem rows and attaching category ratings by column alignment.</doc>
If at least one of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_XX} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_DifferentViewsRated.module_DifferentViewsRated
        
        For each perspective:
            {ITEM_COUNTER} = 1 <doc>{ITEM_COUNTER} is only necessary to create unique IDs.</doc>
            {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} = file where {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_}XX corresponds to the perspective <doc>Here we use the semantic capabilities to map perspective and file. So keep this in mind when creating your naming concept</doc>
            
            <doc>Here we use local variable to iterate through the post-its.</doc>
            First post-it row = Extract text from each post-it in first row of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_IDEA_READ_AREA} from {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            Second post-it row = Extract text from each post-it in second row of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_IDEA_READ_AREA} from {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            {CATEGORY_ROW_01} = Extract text from each post-it in first row of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_RATE_READ_AREA} from {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            {CATEGORY_ROW_02} = Extract text from each post-it in second row of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_RATE_READ_AREA} from {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            {CATEGORY_ROW_03} = Extract text from each post-it in third row of {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_RATE_READ_AREA} from {MD_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            <doc>We start with the first post-it row.</doc>
            For each post-it in First post-it row:
                Create WorkshopItemRated with:
                    id = "ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, perspective + {ITEM_COUNTER})
                    
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it <doc>We add post-it from first row, column x to {TARGET_FILE}.</doc>
                    idea = PostIt

                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from post-it in the second row corresponding to the same column as the idea post-it <doc>We add post-it from second row, column x to {TARGET_FILE}.</doc>
                    problemSolved = PostIt

                    {ITEM_COUNTER} = {ITEM_COUNTER} + 1

                    For each category in categoryRating:
                        categoryRating.rating = number extracted from post-it in {CATEGORY_ROW_XX} corresponding to the same column as the idea post-it <doc>We add post-its from each category row, column x to {TARGET_FILE}.</doc>

                append WorkshopItemRated to Module_DifferentViewsRated.workshopItemRated


<doc>Enrich capability entries with rating and extracted supporting post-it notes per capability area.</doc>
If {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_CapabilityMatrix
        
        For each capability:
            capability.rating = Extract number or value between 2 numbers from {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_RATE_READ_AREA} where line is crossing and which is closest to {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_INFO_READ_AREA_XX}. If the line is crossing between 2 values, take the appropriate decimal value (e.g. if crossing between 3 and 4, take 3.5). If the line is crossing exactly on a number, take that number as rating.

            Extract text from each post-it in {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_INFO_READ_AREA_XX} from {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            For each post-it extracted:
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                append PostIt to capability    
        

<doc>Populate Value/Effort modules per team and classify each extracted idea into a weight category based on location.</doc>
If {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_ValueEffortMatrix.module_ValueEffortMatrix
        
        For each teamName:
            {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} = Rectangle area of the picture where the background color corresponds to teamName.
            {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_BIG_BET} = Rectangle area of post-it size within {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} with text "BIG BET" in the center and directly right to a drawing of a head with a lightbulb
            {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_NO_BRAINER} = Rectangle area with different background color shading within {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA}, containing the text "NO BRAINER". Take only the area with the shading grade that contains the text, not an area with a different shading grade.
            {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_WISE_CHOICE} = Rectangle area with different background color shading within {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA}, containing the text "WISE CHOICE". Take only the area with the shading grade that contains the text, not an area with a different shading grade. The top boundary of this rectangle must be aligned exactly with the top boundary of {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_NO_BRAINER}.
            
            Extract text from each post-it in {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} from {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            For each post-it extracted:
                Create WorkshopItemWeighted with:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    id = "ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, teamName + {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    idea = PostIt

                    If biggest part of post-it is located in {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_BIG_BET}:
                        category = Big Bet
                    Else if biggest part of post-it is located in {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_NO_BRAINER}:
                        category = No Brainer
                    Else if biggest part of post-it is located in {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA_WISE_CHOICE}:
                        category = Wise Choice
                    Else:
                        category = Nice to have

                append WorkshopItemWeighted to Module_ValueEffortMatrix.workshopItemWeighted           
      

<doc>Populate Detailed Working Plan per team, including Big Bet and notes for explanation/resource sections.</doc>
If at least one of {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_XX} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_DetailedWorkingPlan.module_DetailedWorkingPlan
        
        For each teamName:
            {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE} = file where {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_}XX corresponds to the teamName
            
            {BIG_BET} = Extract text from each post-it in {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_READ_AREA_BIG_BET} from {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            bigBet = {BIG_BET}

            For each workplanItemGroupExplanationData.workplanItemOneStep:
                {EXPLANATION_DATA_ONE_STEP} = Extract text from each post-it in {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE} using OCR and light normalization. Post-its located below workplanItemOneStep.topic. Maximum is 4 rows and 2 columns of post-its.

                For each post-it in {EXPLANATION_DATA_ONE_STEP}
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    note = PostIt
                
                append note to workplanItemOneStep.explanationDataOneStep

            For each workplanItemGroupExplanationData.workplanItemTwoStep:
                {EXPLANATION_DATA_TWO_STEP} = Extract text from each post-it in {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE} using OCR and light normalization. Post-its located below workplanItemTwoStep.description. Maximum is 2 rows and 3 columns of post-its.

                For each post-it in {EXPLANATION_DATA_TWO_STEP}
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    note = PostIt
                
                append note to workplanItemTwoStep.explanationDataTwoStep


            For each workplanItemGroupRequiredResources.workplanItemOneStep:
                {REQ_RES_ONE_STEP} = Extract text from each post-it in {MD_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE} using OCR and light normalization. Post-its located below workplanItemOneStep.description. Maximum is 2 rows and 4 columns of post-its.

                For each post-it in {REQ_RES_ONE_STEP}
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    note = PostIt
                
                append note to workplanItemOneStep.requiredResourcesOneStep


<doc>Populate User Journey step notes by matching extracted post-its to nearby journey step descriptions.</doc>
If {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_UserJourney.module_UserJourney
        
        For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA_XX}:
            Extract text from each post-it from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} within {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA_XX} using OCR and light normalization.
            
            For each userJourneyStep:    
                If post-it located near userJourneyStep.description
                
                    For each post-it extracted:
                        {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                        PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                        PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                        append PostIt to Module_UserJourney.userJourneyStep


<doc>Populate Staged Offering Portfolio streams by matching extracted post-its to reading areas.</doc>
If {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_StagedOfferingPortfolio
        
        {SECTION_COUNTER} = 0

        For each portfolioItemGroup:
            {SECTION_COUNTER} = {SECTION_COUNTER} + 1

            {UPPER_READ_AREA} = {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_READ_AREA_XX} WHERE XX = {SECTION_COUNTER} and y between 0% and 50%
            {LOWER_READ_AREA} = {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_READ_AREA_XX} WHERE XX = {SECTION_COUNTER} and y between 50% and 100%
            
            Get first portfolioItem from portfolioItemGroup:
                Extract text from each post-it from {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} within {UPPER_READ_AREA} using OCR and light normalization.
                
                For each post-it extracted:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    note = PostIt

                    append note to portfolioItem

            Get second portfolioItem from portfolioItemGroup:
                Extract text from each post-it from {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} within {LOWER_READ_AREA} using OCR and light normalization.
                
                For each post-it extracted:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    note = PostIt

                    append note to portfolioItem


<doc>Populate Detailed Idea Investment per team.</doc>
If {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_DetailedIdeaInvestment.module_DetailedIdeaInvestment
        
        For each teamName:
            
            {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} = Rectangle area within {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} where the background color corresponds to teamName.
            {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} = 0
            
            For each detailedIdea:
                {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} = {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} + 1
                {DETAILED_IDEA_FIRST_ROW} = Extract text from each post-it in row {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} of {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} from {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
                {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} = {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} + 1
                {DETAILED_IDEA_SECOND_ROW} = Extract text from each post-it in row {IDEA_ROW_COUNTER} of {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} from {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
                {DETAILED_IDEA_COMPLETE} = {DETAILED_IDEA_FIRST_ROW} + {DETAILED_IDEA_SECOND_ROW}
                {DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT} = Rectangle with white dotted line as border, located left from {DETAILED_IDEA_COMPLETE}

                detailedIdea.budget = Calculate the sum of all numbers extracted from {DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT} using OCR and light normalization.

                i = 0
                For each detailedIdeaStep in detailedIdea:
                    i = i + 1
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from post-it(i) in {DETAILED_IDEA_COMPLETE}
                    note = PostIt

                    append note to detailedIdeaStep.note


<doc>Populate Roadmap module.</doc>
If {MD_ROADMAP_FILE} is not empty:
    Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_Roadmap
        
        For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_XX}:
            Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            For each post-it extracted:
                Create roadmapItem with:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    idea = PostIt
                    category = H1
                    wave = XX
                    id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                    
                append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem

        For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_XX}:
            Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            For each post-it extracted:
                Create roadmapItem with:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    idea = PostIt
                    category = H2
                    wave = XX
                    id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                    
                append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem

        For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_XX}:
            Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

            For each post-it extracted:
                Create roadmapItem with:
                    {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                    PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                    PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                    idea = PostIt
                    category = H3
                    wave = XX
                    id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                    
                append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem    